      "reason": "CMIP6 `o2` is stored per unit volume while the user states thresholds and WOA23 oxygen are in micromoles per kilogram, so the OMZ thresholding and oxygen inventory require a unit-conversion step grounded in this fragment.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "CMIP6 `o2` is per volume (`mol m-3`); OMZ thresholds and WOA23 oxygen/AOU are per mass (`µmol kg-1`), so convert model `o2` before any thresholding or model–WOA comparison: `µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000 / ρ`, using the in-situ density field from `compute_potential_density_anomaly` with `ref_pressure=None`.",
        "Compute OMZ volumes and total O2 inventories on the model volume basis with `Σ c · volcello`; for OMZ thickness use layer thickness from `volcello / areacello`, not a density-based conversion."
      ]
    },
